    "result_text": "Full `mvn test` is green (BUILD SUCCESS). The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI redesigned owner identity with a single-file change to keep structural impact minimal.\n\n**Changed:** `src/main/java/.../rest/function/owner/AssignOwnerCustomerCode.java`\n\n`customerCode` is now built as `<REGION>-<HASH8>`:\n- **REGION** \u2014 `Locality.of(owner)`, the existing region-code-from-postcode derivation (e.g. postcode `2000` \u2192 `NSW`).\n- **HASH8** \u2014 the first 8 upper-case hex characters of `SHA-256(normalizedTelephone + lastName)`, where `normalizedTelephone` is the already-E.164-normalized `owner.getTelephone()` set upstream by `BuildOwner`.\n\nThe per-city sequence number (and the `OwnerRepository` lookup it required) is gone entirely.\n\n**Why nothing else needed to change:** every value the spec says must \"move to the new identity\" is already derived from `owner.getCustomerCode()` or `Locality.of(owner)`, so they follow automatically:\n- `MembershipNumber.of` \u2192 `<customerCode>-M<YY>`, reads the code.\n- `CheckDigit.of` \u2192 Luhn over the code's digits.\n- The `AUDIT` log line \u2192 prints `owner.getCustomerCode()`.\n- `locality` (in `OwnerMapper`) \u2192 `Locality.of(owner)`, which is the exact REGION component of the new code, so locality and the code's region are one and the same derivation.\n\nConfirmed by the run: `AUDIT - owner created ... customerCode=NSW-16E6609E`, matching the new-test regex `[A-Z0-9]+-[0-9A-F]{8}`. `AcceptanceTest.coreCustomerCodeIsRegionHash` and the full suite pass (BUILD SUCCESS).",
